{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794843411,"nonce":"z3zQ20my/vaLPoB9dMDvISAf06o=","title":"hxn-audio: low-latency audio output and a mixer that runs natively","message":"hxnme M0. hxn-av decodes and plays files but has no output stream to mix into. The mixer has to run natively: native code may not call a host function, so Haxe sends commands (play, stop, gain, pan, bus routing, effect parameters) and buffers, and the mix runs on the audio thread in Rust. Voices, buses, effects, streamed sources fed by hxn-av's decoders, and device selection and changes. Natively over cpal or the platform APIs (CoreAudio, WASAPI, PipeWire/ALSA, AAudio, AVAudioSession); in the browser an AudioWorklet reading a shared ring.\n\nDone when a program plays overlapping sounds and streamed music on every platform, with a measured output latency.","files":null}]}